ork, and research activities.\",4\r\n272,PC,\"PC refers to personal computers that can connect to the internet via wifi, allowing users to access online resources without cables.\",3\r\n238,INTANSARI RETNANINGRUM,Intansari Retnaningrum is a student discussing the role of hardware and software in her environment.,2\r\n71,HEADSET,\"A headset is an audio output device designed for listening to sound from a computer, functioning as a multimedia sound processing device. It typically includes a microphone, enabling communication in addition to audio listening. The headset serves as an external device that allows users, such as Muhammad Fauzan Rafi, to clearly hear sound and speak during online activities. Overall, a headset is an essential output device that takes sound from a computer, ensuring users can hear audio clearly.\",6\r\n256,INDONESIA,\"Indonesia is a Southeast Asian country where internet access is predominantly facilitated through WiFi, with services provided by Wifi.id. WiFi is widely utilized among the population, making it a common means of connecting to the internet. In addition to internet services, television, informally known as TV, plays a significant role in communication within the country. It has been adopted as a key medium for entertainment and information dissemination, highlighting its importance in Indonesian society.\",4\r\n72,WEBCAM,\"The \"\"WEBCAM\"\" is a versatile device primarily utilized in educational settings to capture and transmit video of the lecture environment for online attendees, facilitating remote learning. It is a small digital camera that serves as a multimedia device for image and video processing, allowing users to take pictures or record videos. Specifically, one notable example is a webcam used by Muhammad Fauzan Rafi, which supports 1080 HD video, ensuring clearer video delivery. Additionally, the webcam functions as an input device that captures images within a certain range and inputs them into a computer, making it